1
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,980
恢弘壮丽.
Colossal beauty.

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:07,380
错综复杂，令人惊叹.
Awe-inspiring intricacy.

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,990
我们宇宙的所有奇观,只是天意造化？
Are the wonders of our universe a cosmic accident

4
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:15,320
还是经过了精妙的设计？
or the result of intelligent design？

5
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:19,590
多少世纪以来, 宗教和科学如同宿敌，争论不休.
For centuries, religion and science were bitter foes.

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,770
如今，科学正在积极搜寻着我们的造物主.
Now science actively searches for our creator.

7
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:27,770
有些物理学家相信他藏身数学.
Some physicists think he's hidden in the math.

8
00:00:27,770 --> 00:00:31,240
神经学专家觉得她在我们的大脑中.
Neurologists think she might be in our brains.

9
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:35,140
编程高手们认为上帝是他们的一员，
And computer coders believe God is one of them

10
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:39,550
而我们的世界，不过是他调试用的模拟器.
and that our world is nothing more than his simulation.

11
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:46,920
空间.
Space.

12
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,390
时间.
Time.

13
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:50,290
生命本身.
Life itself.

14
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:57,170
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

15
00:00:57,170 --> 00:01:00,170
♪穿越虫洞，第1x01集 与摩根.弗里曼同行♪
♪Through the Wormhole 1x01 with Morgan Freeman♪

16
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:03,700
存在造物主吗？
Is There a Creator？

17
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:06,840
每种文化都有自己的神,
every culture claims a God,

18
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,840
全能的实体，
an all-powerful entity

19
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:12,950
创造了世界 安排我们的命运.
that created the world and directs our fate.

20
00:01:12,950 --> 00:01:17,690
我们为何都相信存在造物主？
But why do we share this belief in a cosmic creator？

21
00:01:17,690 --> 00:01:22,060
我们是出于精神或文化的需要 而创造这一概念吗？
Did we dream it up to serve a need in our psyche or culture？

22
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:25,160
神真的 --
Is God really out there --

23
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,030
在上面吗？
up there？

24
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:31,730
这是通向科学之神的旅程
This is a journey into the science of God.

25
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:34,970
我保证，一个不错的旅程
I promise you it's quite a trip.

26
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:39,210
我们会发现一些蔑视信仰的东西.
Some of what we'll find almost defies belief.

27
00:01:41,210 --> 00:01:43,380
20世纪70年代初的某个时间,
Sometime in the early '70s,

28
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:47,150
我给女儿买了个蚂蚁农场.
I bought my daughter an ant farm.

29
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:51,790
她很快就厌烦了，可我们有
She soon got bored, but not me.

30
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:54,620
我对这个小社会印象深刻
I was memorized by this little menagerie

31
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:57,530
在两片玻璃之间的小世界.
squeezed between two panes of glass.

32
00:01:57,530 --> 00:02:01,560
我很好奇，它们会知道我的存在吗，
And I wondered, what could they ever know about me,

33
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:05,170
这个创造了它们世界的家伙？
the one who built their world？

34
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:08,970
我们又如何能了解我们的造物主？,
What can we ever learn about who or what created us,

35
00:02:08,970 --> 00:02:13,540
我们不也被自己的环境所约束？
stranded as we are in this colony of humanity？

36
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,140
长久以来，科学家们
For as long as scientists

37
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:18,580
不遗余力的试图了解我们的世界,
have struggled to understand our place in the universe,

38
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:22,220
有人期望能够有幸看到神， 哪怕只是一瞥
there have been those who've hoped to get a glimpse of God.

39
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:29,960
400年前，伟大的天文学家伽利略
400 years ago, the great astronomer Galileo Galilei

40
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,630
有了一个开创性的深刻见解
had a ground-breaking insight.

41
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:37,070
自然之书是由数学语言挥就的
Nature's grand book is written in the language of mathematics.

42
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:39,070
从那时起,
From that time to this,

43
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:42,870
像牛顿、爱因斯坦这些科学天才，
scientific geniuses like Newton and Einstein

44
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:46,210
把定义物理定理的等式当作工具，
used math to dig deep into the workings of nature,

45
00:02:46,210 --> 00:02:48,410
向深埋的自然之谜掘进，
to search for God

46
00:02:48,410 --> 00:02:52,210
搜寻神的踪迹.
through the equations that defined the laws of physics.

47
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:55,880
加瑞特·里斯是最近有望跻身名人堂
The latest mind hoping to join these illustrious ranks

48
00:02:55,890 --> 00:02:57,890
的一位
is Garrett Lisi.

49
00:02:57,890 --> 00:02:59,190
我们能用数学
The universe

50
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:02,390
成功的描述宇宙.
can very successfully be described mathematically.

51
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:04,630
你会想象我们的世界
You have to imagine how the world's working

52
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:06,460
在必然率的约束之中
in a certain circumstance

53
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:09,100
利用推理和数学就能够
and then use reason and mathematics

54
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:12,330
确定什么会发生.
to develop a description of how that might be happening.

55
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:13,570
但是，
But it's imagination

56
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:16,170
想象并不合理.
that breaks the trail before reason enters.

57
00:03:16,170 --> 00:03:19,610
在获得博士学位后，
After earning his Phd,

58
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:22,680
加瑞特逃离了学术界
Garrett escaped the confines of academia

59
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:26,550
和原来的研究圈子说拜拜了.
in search of adventure and a space in which to think.

60
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:30,390
我不愿从事循规蹈矩的学究工作,
Rather than go into a normal academic-track job,

61
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:33,490
我去了毛伊岛, 没事儿时冲冲浪,
I just split off for Maui, became a surf bum,

62
00:03:33,490 --> 00:03:35,420
并且从事我真正想做的研究
and did the research I wanted to --

63
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:39,430
物理研究和冲浪，这就是我想做的
mostly spent time doing physics research and surfing.

64
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:45,130
我们为了理解自然而做出的种种尝试
But all of our attempts to understand nature

65
00:03:45,130 --> 00:03:48,000
根本不是一个整体，而是七零八落.
so far have been fragmentary.

66
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,470
对原子，我们建立一套规则
There's one set of rules for tiny atoms,

67
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:54,210
对宏观物理，比如星球和星系， 我们又建立一套.
another for giant objects like stars and galaxies.

68
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:58,280
两套规则的数学原理并不相容.
And the two sets of math don't fit together.

69
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:01,050
里斯这样的物理学家们
What physicists like Lisi seek

70
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:03,950
正是寻找一个统一的理论,
is a single, overarching theory,

71
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:08,460
一个数学设计，能够解释所有的现象.
a mathematical design that explains everything.

72
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:11,730
加瑞特认为 他已经找到了
Garrett thinks he may at last have found

73
00:04:11,730 --> 00:04:15,400
这个适用于万物的理论.
this theory of everything.

74
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:19,870
如果他是对的，神也许是个很棒的数学家.
And if he's right, God could be one heck of a mathematician.

75
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:23,810
加瑞特的工作处在物理研究的前沿
Garrett's work is at a leading edge of physics.

76
00:04:23,810 --> 00:04:27,610
在我们被复杂的数学，搞得七荤八素之前,
Before we plunge into this mind-bending math,

77
00:04:27,610 --> 00:04:31,010
我们先缓一缓,
we first need to back up a bit,

78
00:04:31,010 --> 00:04:33,420
也许已经有证据表明
because it's possible

79
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:36,550
造物主就在数学之中
there's already evidence for a creator in the math.

80
00:04:38,890 --> 00:04:42,260
安迪.阿尔布雷克特，一个顶尖的宇宙学家
Andy Albrecht is a leading cosmologist.

81
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:45,060
哈喽, 你好吗？
Hello, how are you？

82
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:48,000
他也是一个声名卓著的巧克力狂
He's also a renowned chocoholic.

83
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,000
我要巧克力酥和拿铁咖啡
I'll have the chocolate soufflé and a latte.

84
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,870
如同一个完美的巧克力酥
Just as a perfect chocolate soufflé

85
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:58,410
原料完美的混合
relies on a precise mixture of ingredients

86
00:04:58,410 --> 00:05:02,040
在特定的温度，烘焙特定的时间
baked at a specific temperature for an exact time,

87
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,880
我们的宇宙也是如此
so our universe looks the way it does

88
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:09,820
在四种基本力量间，达成了精确的平衡
because of a precise balance between four fundamental forces.

89
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:12,020
四种我们熟知并热爱的力量
The four forces we know and love

90
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,620
就在你我身边
in the world around us

91
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:16,190
它们是：重力，电磁力
are gravity, electromagnetism --

92
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:18,430
以上两位您以前可能听说过.
those you've probably heard of.

93
00:05:18,430 --> 00:05:21,230
剩下的两位是弱相互作用和强相互作用
Then there's also the weak force and the strong force.

94
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:23,300
有点耳生？显得很专业吧？
They're a little bit more specialized

95
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:24,600
但是却是保证我们世界正常运转的
but absolutely essential

96
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,740
不可缺少的力量
to make the world work the way it does.

97
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:29,840
重力，一般来说
Gravity, in many ways,

98
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,940
是我们最早有所体会的
is the force we know first.

99
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:33,980
我们蹒跚学步, 然后摔跤
We try to walk, and we fall down.

100
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,480
正是重力在玩儿我们
That's because of gravity.

101
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,480
如果你搬了什么重东西,摔了
When you carry something a little too heavy and it falls,

102
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,380
又是重力在搞鬼
it's because of gravity.

103
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:43,390
电磁理论，使我们了解物质的化学性质
Electromagnetism tells us how the chemistry works.

104
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:46,920
在你做饭时, 你所用的能量
When you cook something, the energy you use

105
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:50,590
归根结底是电磁能
is ultimately electromagnetic energy.

106
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,660
弱相互作用要比电磁力弱
Weak force is about a billion times less strong

107
00:05:55,670 --> 00:05:57,570
大概只有电磁力的10亿分之一
than electromagnetism,

108
00:05:57,570 --> 00:06:01,270
它与辐射能有关
and it's responsible for radioactivity.

109
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:04,640
香蕉里的钾就有放射性
The potassium in a banana is radioactive.

110
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:09,680
如果放射性太强, 我们就会死亡
If the rate were too high, it could destroy us.

111
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:12,710
本质上，太阳就是个核反应堆
The sun is basically a nuclear reactor.

112
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:15,950
强相互作用在核反应过程中释放能量
The strong forces release energy in the nuclear reactions.

113
00:06:15,950 --> 00:06:20,290
值得注意的是,这四种作用加载一起
One of the remarkable things is, when you add it all up,

114
00:06:20,290 --> 00:06:23,160
就构成了
all these forces have to be exactly the way they are

115
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:25,330
我们生活中的所有力
for life as we know it to exist.

116
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:28,160
改变它们中的任何一个, 调整一下参数
Change any one of them, dial the parameters,

117
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:30,170
就会出现某种错误--
and something will go wrong --

118
00:06:30,170 --> 00:06:32,400
地球就没有了,
the planet will disappear,

119
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,970
太阳也消亡了,
the sun will shut down,

120
00:06:34,970 --> 00:06:38,110
DNA变得一塌糊涂.
the DNA will come unraveled.

121
00:06:38,110 --> 00:06:41,640
有些人称之为 "金发姑娘范式"--
Some people call it the Goldilocks paradigm --

122
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:45,480
一点不多，一点不少，所有一切都是刚刚好.
not too much, not too little, everything's just right.

123
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,120
噢,太完美了.
Oh, that's perfect.

124
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:50,890
有些物理学家相信
Some physicists believe

125
00:06:50,890 --> 00:06:55,390
这些作用力的完美配比正是神之证据
this precise calibration of forces is evidence of God.

126
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:59,330
John Polkinghorne博士是从事夸克研究的先锋,
Dr. John Polkinghorne did pioneering work on the quark,

127
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:02,400
夸克,一类基本粒子.
a fundamental subatomic particle.

128
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:08,140
他还是位不列颠帝国的二级爵士,一位Sir.
He is also a knight commander of the British Empire, a Sir.

129
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:10,640
他的前半生，一直在进行
And after a lifetime

130
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:12,940
令人尊敬的科学探寻,
of distinguished scientific inquiry,

131
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:16,510
现在，他致力于另一项工作...
he was inspired to follow a new line of work...

132
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:19,680
做一个牧师.
As a priest.

133
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,880
俺真的相信上帝,真的,不忽悠你.
I do indeed believe in God, yes, indeed.

134
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:23,990
是的,实际上,我是个圣公会牧师
Yes, in fact, I'm an Anglican priest,

135
00:07:23,990 --> 00:07:26,120
所以,如果我不信主,那才是令人震惊的事儿呢.
so it would be rather shocking if I didn't.

136
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:31,390
这四种作用力组合万物
Those four fundamental forces are the portfolio of things

137
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:34,160
引导了物理研究的进程.
that bring about the physical processes of the world.

138
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,660
有一个有趣的事实
And a very interesting fact about the world

139
00:07:36,670 --> 00:07:38,000
这四种各有特性基本作用的真实性质,
is that those forces,

140
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,640
应该和我们的观测结果
in their specific strengths that they have,

141
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:43,610
很接近,
have to be very close to what we actually observe

142
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:46,270
如果我们能从这儿观测的话,
if we were to be here to observe them,

143
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:48,910
因为证据显示,我们这个炭基生命的世界
because it turns out that only a world

144
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:52,810
之所以能够存在的基础
whose forces are very similar to the ones that we experience

145
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:55,780
正是这四种作用关系.
would be capable of producing carbon-based life.

146
00:07:55,790 --> 00:07:58,550
John觉得很难想象这样的事实
John finds it difficult to imagine

147
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:00,960
我们如此精妙的宇宙
that the fine-tuning of our universe

148
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,960
只不过是巧合的后果,
has happened by accident,

149
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:06,130
而没有神意的主使.
that there is no divine hand behind it.

150
00:08:06,130 --> 00:08:09,860
这种精妙明示了,我们并不是 生活在任何旧世界
This fine-tuning makes it clear we don't live in any old world.

151
00:08:09,870 --> 00:08:11,830
我们生活在 一个非常特殊的宇宙中.
We live in a very particular universe.

152
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:15,440
这是为什么？ 为什么我们如此幸运？
And why is that？ Why are we so lucky？

153
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:18,440
当然, 宗教会给你一个
Of course, religious belief offers you

154
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:21,940
非常直白 非常有吸引力的解释.
a very straightforward and attractive explanation.

155
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:24,380
但是科学家们
But scientists are split

156
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:26,850
对这种平衡是来自预先设计的看法
over whether this balance of forces

157
00:08:26,850 --> 00:08:29,080
存在异议.
is a sign of intelligent design.

158
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:32,290
实际上, 现在的宇宙也许
In fact, it could be nothing more

159
00:08:32,290 --> 00:08:34,490
只是像掷骰子一样的偶然后果.
than a roll of the cosmic dice.

160
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:39,630
Alan Guth博士 宇宙学权威.
Dr. Alan Guth is a revered figure in cosmology.

161
00:08:39,630 --> 00:08:41,630
他的宇宙膨胀理论
His theory of inflation

162
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:45,470
是关于早期宇宙形成的主流理论.
is the accepted idea of how the early universe formed.

163
00:08:45,470 --> 00:08:49,140
宇宙膨胀说的是 在大爆炸之后,
Inflation says that right after the big bang,

164
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:52,440
宇宙扩展的非常快,
the universe expanded phenomenally fast,

165
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:57,710
在几分之一秒内膨胀了10万倍.
doubling in size 100,000 times in just a fraction of a second.

166
00:08:57,710 --> 00:08:59,780
膨胀理论解释了
Inflation helps explain

167
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:03,590
我们所知的世界如何形成并存在.
how the world we know could have come into existence.

168
00:09:03,590 --> 00:09:07,190
可是膨胀理论有另一层含义 --
But inflation has another head-spinning implication --

169
00:09:07,190 --> 00:09:10,630
那就是可能有不同的宇宙.
there ought to be more than one universe.

170
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:16,700
膨胀过程的一个重要特性是
An important feature of this process of inflation

